,rakishness:bt,pathic:xt,glycolic:St,zirconate:Ct,colleterial:wt,oblong:Tt,"schoharie grit":`The formation belonging to the middle of the three subdivisions of the Corniferous period in the American Devonian system; -- so called from Schoharie, in New York, where it occurs. See the Chart of Geology.`,spelter:Et,inclined:Dt,tycoon:Ot,"fop-doodle":`A stupid or insignaficant fellow; a fool; a simpleton. [R.] Hudibras.`,correspondently:kt,saneness:At,ciliiform:jt,yakin:Mt,invalued:Nt,plucked:Pt,metaphysic:Ft,townlet:It,ustion:Lt,anniversary:Rt,crapula:zt,"lozenge-shaped":`Having the form of a lozenge or rhomb. The lozenged panes of a very small latticed window. C. Bronté.`,echinid:Bt,size:Vt,comportment:Ht,tabanus:Ut,cundurango:Wt,termonology:Gt,yttria:Kt,ciliata:qt,dak:Jt,sleighty:Yt,uberous:Xt,planetoidal:Zt,tramroad:Qt,sandish:$t,enatation:en,jansenism:tn,"chance-medley":`1. (Law)  The kiling of another in self-defense upon a sudden and unpremeditated encounter. See Chaud-Medley. Note: The term has been sometimes applied to any kind of homicide by misadventure, or to any accidental killing of a person without premeditation or evil intent, but, in strictness, is applicable to such killing as happens in defending one's self against assault. Bouvier. 2. Luck; chance; accident. Milton. Cowper.`,potoroo:nn,shellproof:rn,stomatiferous:an,mistell:on,pathematic:sn,piedouche:cn,slow:ln,pipestem:un,hardpan:dn,notably:fn,preparatory:pn,fleshings:mn,incontinence:hn,thief:gn,"water supply":`A supply of water; specifically, water collected, as in reservoirs, and conveyed, as by pipes, for use in a city, mill, or the like.`,circumduction:_n,dispurvey:vn,denouncer:yn,cytoblast:bn,sleeveless:xn,restagnation:Sn,retexture:Cn,suade:wn,aromatous:Tn,slatting:En,detonate:Dn,seizable:On,decerptible:kn,chanfrin:An,gnathotheca:jn,aporosa:Mn,ringtail:Nn,trunnioned:Pn,cabriole:Fn,endurance:In,quaily:Ln,topsoil:Rn,assagai:zn,oratorio:Bn,fleetings:Vn,inflammative:Hn,gregarinae:Un,oculomotor:Wn,re